<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gebhard Leberecht von Blücher</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1742">1742</a>–<a href="/years/1819">1819</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Blücher, Prince Blücher of Wahlstatt, Prince Blücher von Wahlstatt, Marshal Forwards</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gebhard Leberecht von Blücher (1742–1819) was a Prussian field marshal of the Napoleonic Wars. Known as Marshal Forwards, he won the Battle of the Katzbach and fought at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> in 1813, then led his army across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. In 1815, after defeat at Ligny, his arrival on the field at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a> was decisive in the final defeat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gebhard-leberecht-von-blucher.jpg" alt="Gebhard Leberecht von Blücher" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Dawe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Field_Marshal_Prince_von_Blucher.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
